00000000                             1  *--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
00000000                             2  * Title      :  PROJECT1 IRONBOUND
00000000                             3  * Written by :  Callum Matthews C00306572
00000000                             4  * Date       :  Started on the 19th of February. 
00000000                             5  * Description:  An alternative physics game where gravity works against you. Collect scrap metal to weigh yourself down, and fight off enemies competing for the same resources.
00000000                             6  *
00000000                             7  * Issues encountered: When loading health or mass into D1, it would show a number like 65000. This is because MOVE.B only overwrites lower 8 bits of D1.
00000000                             8  * Resolution:   To resolve, I used CLR.W D1 to set the lower 16 bits of D1 to 0, basically removing any garbage from earlier that was there, ensuring I can print or store only the value i need.
00000000                             9  *               I did not use AI to resolve this issue. It was a very simple fix, i just forgot to clear the registers when i started writing this program.
00000000                            10  *
00000000                            11  * IMPORTANT NOTE: As can be seen under my variables, i store enemy health as an array, and each day we take a value from that array to give to the enemy we encounter. The enemy health depends on what day you are on.
00000000                            12  *                 As each day you can choose whether to stay home or venture out, you may not encounter an enemy depending on this choice.
00000000                            13  *                 Therefore, i need to chose enemy health from this array based off what day you are on. I could not figure this out myself, and ran into errors when assembling, and this was my major hurdle.
00000000                            14  *                 I also needed help resolving a random number. My plan was to use time trap 8 to get time since midnight, which is different every time game is ran, but it returned a very long number.
00000000                            15  *                 I needed to trim it down so its easier to allocate chance, so by making it a number 0 - 99, 100 numbers, i could set different ranges as different chances. 0 - 9 is 10%, 10 - 19 is 10% and so on.
00000000                            16  *
00000000                            17  * Resoltion:      To resolve this array issue, and the time issue, i had to use AI to get help. The four subroutines that needed AI help are as follows:
00000000                            18  *
00000000                            19  *                 GET_ENEMY_HP
00000000                            20  *                 HP_LOOP
00000000                            21  *                 HP_FOUND
00000000                            22  *                 RANDOM_0_99 ------> i planned on using the time trap 8 regardless, just needed to figure out how to go about trimming number as time will give me a different number each time game is ran, appearing random
00000000                            23  *
00000000                            24  *                 I do now understand how these subroutines work. I have comments beside them explaining as such. However, it took AI help to explain how to go about navigating the array based off day, as i wanted to do.
00000000                            25  *                 I felt it nesisary to highlight that these subroutines were AI assisted.
00000000                            26  *                 For these four subroutines mentioned above, the AI used was ChatGpt. 
00000000                            27  *                 I did not use it beyond the aforementioned subroutines above.
00000000                            28  *
00000000                            29  * Known bugs:   As of now, I have no confirmed known bugs. My main issue was not clearing registers and the issue with my choice to base enemy health off an array These are now both resolved.
00000000                            30  *               I also had gameplay loop issues with random events messages printing, but now resolved.
00000000                            31  *               However, random event selection works from time, with the trap task 8. So theoretically, event chance can be based off the time at which you run the code? I havent had issues with this, but i beleive that it could provide an issue?
